# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Our Story -- Firebase Configuration
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your credentials.
# NEVER commit .env.local to git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Go to https://console.firebase.google.com → Your project → Project settings → Your apps
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key_here
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=123456789
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:123456789:web:abc123

# Push notifications (optional — the app works fine without this, you just
# won't get notified when it's closed). Go to Project settings → Cloud
# Messaging → Web configuration → Web Push certificates → Generate key pair.
VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=

# The app itself never uses a Firebase Auth password — see
# functions/index.js's signInAsPartner, which verifies the birthday
# server-side and mints a sign-in token, so no static credential ever ships
# in the client bundle (this repo deploys to public URLs — GitHub Pages,
# Vercel — where anything baked into a build is extractable by anyone who
# opens dev tools, no matter how random the value is).
#
# These two vars are ONLY used by the local admin scripts in scripts/
# (seeding/resetting Firestore data) — never read by the app, never shipped
# to any build. Generate real random values once, e.g. `openssl rand -base64
# 24`, and set them on the two accounts in Authentication → Users. Leave
# blank if you're not using those scripts.
VITE_FIREBASE_HIM_PASSWORD=
VITE_FIREBASE_HER_PASSWORD=

# App Check (optional but recommended — protects signInAsPartner from being
# hammered by anything other than this actual app; see src/lib/firebase.ts).
# Firebase Console → App Check → Apps → your web app → Register → reCAPTCHA v3
# → paste the generated site key here. Leave blank to skip App Check entirely
# (the app works fine without it, this is a hardening layer, not a
# requirement). See step 8 below for the full one-time setup.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS (one-time, takes ~10 minutes)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Go to firebase.google.com → Create project "our-story" → Continue
#    (Disable Google Analytics, not needed)
#
# 2. Add a Web app → nickname "our-story-web" → Register app
#    Copy the config values into this file above.
#
# 3. Authentication
#    Left sidebar → Authentication → Sign-in method → Email/Password → Enable → Save
#
# 4. Firestore Database
#    Left sidebar → Firestore Database → Create database
#    Choose: Production mode → Next
#    Location: africa-south1 (Johannesburg) → Enable
#    Rules are NOT pasted here by hand — they live in firestore.rules at the
#    repo root and deploy with:
#      firebase deploy --only firestore:rules
#    That file restricts access to exactly the two partner accounts by email.
#    Do not replace it with a rule that grants access to any authenticated
#    user — that lets anyone who self-registers a Firebase account read and
#    write all of this app's data.
#
# 5. Storage
#    Left sidebar → Storage → Get started → Production mode → Next
#    Same region (africa-south1) → Done
#    Rules likewise live in storage.rules at the repo root and deploy with:
#      firebase deploy --only storage
#
# 6. Push notifications (optional, needed only for background/closed-app
#    message + call alerts)
#    - Requires the Blaze (pay-as-you-go) billing plan — Cloud Functions
#      don't run at all on the free Spark plan. Settings → Usage and
#      billing → Modify plan. Real usage cost for two people: ~$0/month.
#    - Project settings → Cloud Messaging → Web configuration →
#      Web Push certificates → Generate key pair → paste into
#      VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY above.
#    - Deploy the Cloud Function that actually sends the pushes:
#        cd functions && npm install && cd ..
#        firebase deploy --only functions
#
# 7. The two partner accounts (phathu@ourstory.app, lihle@ourstory.app) need
#    to exist once in Authentication → Users before anyone can sign in —
#    signInAsPartner (step 6's function deploy) looks them up by email but
#    doesn't create them. Add them manually with any real random password
#    (the app never uses it; only the scripts/ admin tools do, see above).
#
# 8. App Check (optional, hardens signInAsPartner against automated abuse)
#    - Firebase Console → App Check → Apps → register your web app →
#      reCAPTCHA v3 → paste the site key into VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY above.
#    - Run `npm run dev` once with that key set — the browser console logs a
#      debug token (real reCAPTCHA keys don't validate on localhost). Copy
#      it into Firebase Console → App Check → your app → "Manage debug
#      tokens" → Add. One-time per dev machine.
#    - The same reCAPTCHA v3 key works inside the native Android build too
#      (Capacitor's WebView can run it like any other web content) — no
#      separate native setup needed.
#    - IMPORTANT: enforceAppCheck is NOT turned on for signInAsPartner yet
#      even after you do the above — see the comment on that function in
#      functions/index.js for why, and do a full login test on BOTH web and
#      the native APK before ever flipping that flag on. Turning it on
#      before every client is actually sending valid tokens would lock both
#      partners out of login entirely.
#
# That is it! Run: npm run dev
#
# Everything (chat, letters, dreams, memories, photos) syncs through Firebase.
